{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-165866",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, we recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-2)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x-2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
